In 2002, the film ranked #19 on AFI's 100 Years... 100 Passions.
In March 2025, feminist art critic Jan Lisa Huttner honored Demi Moore at SWAN Day 2025 events in New York City and Chicago for her performances in Ghost and The Substance, the film which later earned her the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy Huttner wrote:…when I watched Ghost again, I saw something I wasn’t even looking for in the Wayback: "Molly Jensen" – the character Demi plays in Ghost – is a sculptor preparing for her first public exhibition? What a perfect fit… "Molly Jensen" is now recognized worldwide as one of Demi’s most iconic roles. So high time to celebrate Demi’s courage, resilience, and, yes, persistence.
